.TH MOUTHTYPE-LINUX 1 "" "mouthtype-linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mouthtype-linux \- local voice dictation client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mouthtype-linux
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Records only after an explicit start, transcribes on this machine and delivers the text to the focused window.
Common commands are \fBserve\fR, \fBstart\fR, \fBstop\fR, \fBtoggle\fR, \fBcancel\fR, \fBstatus\fR, \fBdoctor\fR and \fBrecover\fR.
Run \fBmouthtype-linux \-\-help\fR for the full list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mouthtype/speech-candidate/linux.json
Client configuration written by \fBmouthtype-linux-setup\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mouthtype-linux-setup (1),
.I /usr/lib/mouthtype-linux/tools/linux-desktop/README.md
